      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Pamela Nel of Patrick Leonard Wilson & Keenan Estates are proud to present Ballyhooly Lodge/ Castle Tavern to the market—a truly exceptional landmark property offering history, character and outstanding potential in one of North Cork's most picturesque settings.\r\n\r\nSet in the heart of Ballyhooly village, just 10 minutes from Fermoy and 20 minutes from Mallow, this remarkable residence overlooks the River Blackwater with breathtaking views towards the iconic Ballyhooly Castle. Nestled in the foothills of the Nagle Mountains and surrounded by the beauty of the Blackwater Valley, this is a rare opportunity to acquire a property that combines lifestyle, heritage and exciting future possibilities.\r\n\r\nOriginally known as the Castle Tavern, Ballyhooly Lodge has been lovingly cared for by its current owners , evolving into a substantial family home while retaining its unique period charm. One of the property's standout features is the former dance hall, now beautifully converted into a peaceful yoga studio, offering a versatile space for wellness, creative pursuits or alternative uses.\r\n\r\nThe property offers 9 bedrooms with potential for a 10th bedroom and 6,5 bathrooms, included in this is a substantial self-contained five-bedroom guest accommodation wing, creating excellent flexibility for extended family living or guest accommodation. Subject to the necessary planning permission, buyers may wish to explore opportunities for further residential use or reconfiguration.\r\n\r\nBeyond the property itself, Ballyhooly is renowned for its rich heritage and unspoilt natural surroundings. Castleblagh Woods sits on the doorstep, providing scenic woodland walks and riverside trails, while the surrounding area is home to many of Cork's most fascinating historical sites, including Labacallee Wedge Tomb, Bridgetown Priory, Glenville Mass Rock, Doonpeter Holy Well and Famine Walk, and the Nano Nagle Birthplace.\r\n\r\nFor buyers seeking to restore and enhance a historic property, Ballyhooly Lodge may be eligible for a range of government-supported schemes, subject to eligibility and approval. \r\n\r\nPurchasers are advised to make their own enquiries regarding available supports and planning requirements.\r\n\r\nWhether you are searching for a distinctive family residence, a boutique guest accommodation opportunity, a wellness retreat, or a unique lifestyle investment, Ballyhooly Lodge offers an exceptional opportunity to create something truly special in an unforgettable setting.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\n\r\nLandmark period property with exceptional character and history\r\n\r\nApproximately 9 bedrooms with potential for a 10th bedroom and 6,5 bathrooms .\r\n\r\nWhich includes a Self-contained five-bedroom guest accommodation wing\r\n\r\nFormer Castle Tavern with a rich local heritage\r\n\r\nSpacious yoga studio converted from the original dance hall\r\n\r\nStunning views overlooking Ballyhooly Castle and the River Blackwater\r\n\r\nPrime village location just 10 minutes from Fermoy and 20 minutes from Mallow\r\n\r\nCastleblagh Woods and scenic woodland walks on the doorstep\r\n\r\nIdeal for multi-generational living, guest accommodation or a wellness venture (subject to planning permission)\r\n\r\nPotential for further development or reconfiguration (subject to planning permission)\r\n\r\nSeparate workshop\r\n\r\nBER D1 efficient rating \r\n\r\nAmple on-site parking\r\n\r\nClose to renowned heritage attractions throughout the Blackwater Valley\r\n\r\nPotential eligibility for renovation, conservation and heritage grant schemes (subject to qualifying criteria)\r\n\r\nEarly Viewing is advised and to appreciate the full potential of this unique property.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
